<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:concept="com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.concept"
  xmlns:mbml="com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.mbml">

  <name>MbmlOverview</name>
  <type>mbml:MbmlOverview</type>
  <baseType>core:Documentation</baseType>
  <is>A guide to MBML authoring in MachineBlocks</is>

  <documentation>
    MBML (MachineBlocks Markup Language) is the declarative authoring format for MachineBlocks.
    It is BML specialized for the MachineBlocks domain: blocks, sets, presets, and composition
    described as typed XML without OpenSCAD knowledge.

    The MBML compiler produces MBOM — the canonical MachineBlocks Object Model. MBOM extends BOM
    Core with MachineBlocks types, native properties, and domain block kinds. Render targets
    interpret MBOM; they do not redefine the domain model.

    Authoring flow: write .bml sources → compile to MBOM → render with a registered target
    (reference: machineblocks-v3-scad). Direct .scad Block Files bypass MBML/MBOM and remain an
    advanced path; prefer MBML for new domain content.
  </documentation>

  <references>
    <see type="mbml:DomainModel" relation="ReadNext">
      Next — Block, NativeBlock, CompositeBlock, Set, Step.
    </see>
    <see type="concept:Architecture" relation="SeeAlso">
      Layered architecture this authoring path sits in.
    </see>
    <see file="docs/02_mbml.md" relation="AuthoringGuide">
      BlockML / BML format rules used by MBML.
    </see>
    <see file="docs/03_mbom.md" relation="DeepDive">
      MBOM domain specialization.
    </see>
  </references>

</block>
